From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Spindler <richard@lateralblast.com.au>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 30/55] packet: decide whether the MAC is enabled for each
 direction, from its name

ssh->none_mac was set by kex_choose_conf() when either direction had the none
cipher and the none MAC, was never cleared, and ssh_set_newkeys() read it for
both directions. A none/none result in one direction therefore switched off
the MAC in the other, and it stayed off after a rekey that went back to a real
cipher.

ssh_set_newkeys() now enables the MAC of each direction unless that
direction's MAC is "none" (kex_choose_conf() only chooses that with the none
cipher after authentication), and kex_choose_conf() clears ssh->none and
ssh->none_mac at the start of each negotiation.
---
 kex.c    | 4 ++++
 packet.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kex.c b/kex.c
index 6315d4558..229a90a9f 100644
--- a/kex.c
+++ b/kex.c
@@ -1068,6 +1068,10 @@ kex_choose_conf(struct ssh *ssh, uint32_t seq)
 	auth_flag = packet_authentication_state(ssh);
 	debug("AUTH STATE IS %d", auth_flag);
 
+	/* these describe this negotiation, not an earlier one */
+	ssh->none = 0;
+	ssh->none_mac = 0;
+
 	debug2("local %s KEXINIT proposal", kex->server ? "server" : "client");
 	if ((r = kex_buf2prop(kex->my, NULL, &my)) != 0)
 		goto out;
diff --git a/packet.c b/packet.c
index 35472fb20..56dd0d042 100644
--- a/packet.c
+++ b/packet.c
@@ -1098,7 +1098,7 @@ ssh_set_newkeys(struct ssh *ssh, int mode)
 	/* if we are using NONE MAC then we don't need to enable the
 	 * mac routines. This disables them and we can claw back some cycles
 	 * from the CPU -cjr 3/21/2023 */
-	if (ssh->none_mac != 1)
+	if (mac->name == NULL || strcmp(mac->name, "none") != 0)
 		mac->enabled = 1;
 
 	DBG(debug_f("cipher_init: %s", dir));
